From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:47:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] service: answer game license requests.

GAME_LICENSE_REQUEST (100) carries a title's Store product id and market. The service finds the
title's package in the display catalog and asks the licensing service for a license to its
content with the device's and the user's MSA tokens, as xodus-cli's license command does.
GAME_LICENSE_RESPONSE (101) says whether the license is active, whether it is a trial, and the
SKU the Store licenses; an account that does not own the title gets an inactive license, and a
failure to find out an HRESULT. xgameruntime's XStoreQueryGameLicense uses it.

Original work for macrock (GPL-3.0-only, as Xodus).

Topic: game-license
